## How to play

- **Tap or click either side** to turn it that way.
- **Hold ← or →** on a keyboard to spin it up.
- **Five quick taps** light it up: ten seconds of fire. Keep steering while it burns.
- It watches your cursor. Space pauses, R resets. Sound and calm motion sit top right.

## What I built

Twelve arms, each hand holding a different gesture, around a face whose eyes follow you and blink. All of it is built from code with three.js geometry; no imported models.

The spin runs on its own small physics model: drag, torque, speed caps and a turbo mode, stepped at 120 Hz so it feels the same on any screen.

Every sound is made live with Web Audio: a thump on each tap, and a roar with a laugh while it burns.

No WebGL2? It falls back to a flat canvas version of the same sculpture.
